# bend-rig: the bending rig (decision C19). The DIP in the vise legs up.
# The arm slides the resistor's lead 2 into the rig 3 mm from the body:
# the clamp and anvil close on it from opposite sides and the former
# bends it down round the mandrel; the rig's shear cuts it to 8 mm. Then
# lead 1 the same way, 12 mm from the body, sheared to a 4 mm end, which
# the arm lays alongside pin 3's leg (a lap joint, decision C22); the
# iron station solders it.
reset circuit=lap
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=180,0,90
vise close
release A U1
pick A R1 grasp=body
lift A mm=60
insert A on=R1.2 at=3
scope aim=R1.2 zoom=3
form angle=90
lift A mm=30
shear A on=R1.2 at=8
lift A mm=60
insert A on=R1.1 at=12
form angle=90
lift A mm=30
shear A on=R1.1 at=17.2
lift A mm=60
bring A R1.1 to=U1.3.tip along=-0.934,0.356,0 lap=3.2
pinch P1 on=R1.1 at=3
release A R1
lift A mm=60
present U1.3+R1.1 at=S1
scope aim=U1.3+R1.1 zoom=8
touch S1 at=U1.3+R1.1 dwell=2
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.3+R1.1 below=100
inspect U1.3+R1.1
unpinch P1
